[h1]Belt Walkie-Talkie[/h1]

[b]Build 42.21 · Singleplayer & Multiplayer · Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3694097672]TooltipLib[/url][/b]

Hook your walkie-talkie on your belt and keep listening. In vanilla, a walkie-talkie on the belt cannot be tuned, switches off as soon as its window is open and hears nothing in singleplayer. This mod fixes that, with your hands free.

[h2]What it does[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Device Options[/b] on a walkie-talkie hooked on the belt: tune it, switch it on, set the volume.
[*]Its window no longer switches it off, even while you take it in hand.
[*][b]Singleplayer:[/b] a switched-on walkie-talkie on the belt hears the station it is tuned to (vanilla stations, emergency broadcast, stations added by mods), with the radio bubble above your character. Storms scramble it like a walkie-talkie in hand.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] a line received by a walkie-talkie hooked on your belt also shows in a radio bubble above your character, not only in the radio chat.
[*]The battery drains at the belt, as in hand.
[*][b]Noise:[/b] a switched-on walkie-talkie at the belt makes a noise that attracts zombies each time it receives a line, as in hand (same volume and range, none with headphones).
[*][b]Mains power:[/b] with Electrical 1, a screwdriver, 2 electronics scraps and 1 electric wire, adapt a walkie-talkie, a HAM radio or the military backpack radio. In an electrified area (generator, or grid power inside a building), its battery no longer drains and recharges, even switched off. A battery must still be inside. The item tooltip shows it.
[/list]

[h2]What it does not do[/h2]

[list]
[*]You cannot transmit from the belt: take the walkie-talkie in hand (or wear a radio on your back) to talk.
[*]A radio stored in your inventory or in a bag hears nothing in singleplayer, as in vanilla.
[/list]

[h2]Sandbox options[/h2]

Page [b]Belt Walkie-Talkie[/b], all on by default; turned off, each one gives back the vanilla behaviour, even in the middle of a game:
[list]
[*]Bubble for a walkie-talkie on the belt (multiplayer).
[*]Battery drain at the belt.
[*]Listening at the belt (singleplayer).
[*]Noise of a walkie-talkie at the belt.
[/list]
Mains recharge time: hours for an empty battery to fill up (10 by default).

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*]Shared receiver of [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811752923]Military Drop[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3813648615]Operation Artemis[/url]: from their next update, they use it when it is enabled.
[*]Better Walkie Talkies is supported: it keeps its own battery and voice handling.
[*]Other mods can add their stations and colours through a small Lua API.
[/list]

Source code (MIT) on [url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/BeltRadio]GitHub[/url].

